schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-process-04-edge-integration-state-accessibility
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-process
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: edge-integration-state-accessibility
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook runtime engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.Process. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize safe integration, dead-process handling, accessibility, and bounded tracing.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.Process edge/integration cell that handles an application that may not be started, a supervisor name that may be missing, and pids that may die between discovery and rendering. Provide a fallback local supervisor tree, guarded app_tree/2 or sup_tree/2 rendering, a safe seq_trace/2 example, and a diagnostics table built with Process.info/2 and Kino.DataTable.

    Requirements: document Livebook compatibility, attached-node assumptions, snapshot state, and process metric data shape; include accessible summaries and fallback status; do not call non-existent Kino.Process.info/1 or memory_usage/0; include safe execution checks for production tracing, remote nodes, dead pids, unbounded Process.list, credentials, eval, shell calls, and sensitive process names.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-process-edge-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino, uses app_tree/2 or sup_tree/2 safely, and builds diagnostics with Process.info/2."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino, attached-node assumptions, and snapshot behavior."
  - "Reactive state: refresh or trace behavior is explicit, bounded, and safe for local examples."
  - "Data shape: app atom, supervisor name or pid, process metric fields, dead-pid status, and trace messages are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: diagnostics table, text summaries, fallback local tree, and status labels are readable."
  - "Safe execution: no fake Kino.Process metric APIs, production-wide tracing, remote credential access, eval, shell commands, unbounded process scans, or sensitive-name leakage."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and guards missing apps, supervisors, and dead pids."
    - "Kino.Process and Process.info APIs are used correctly."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements edge handling for missing apps, missing supervisors, dead pids, tracing, diagnostics, and fallback trees."
    - "Accurately documents Livebook attached-node and snapshot constraints."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Users can tell whether a real app tree, fallback tree, or diagnostic state is being shown."
    - "Process names and metrics are readable without exposing sensitive details unnecessarily."
    - "Trace and tree outputs are scoped for legibility."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles missing apps, dead pids, stopped supervisors, empty traces, high mailbox values, and permission boundaries."
    - "Keeps scans, traces, and refreshes bounded."
    - "Documents production and remote-node risks clearly."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.Process-centered and treats runtime introspection as a sensitive boundary."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-process
- edge-integration-state-accessibility
